# QA M3, Stage 4: a thrown Hackl shatters a falling rock (D-056: both
# gone, 50 points). Falkenstein's rocks come before its H-box, so a Hackl
# at the rocks needs a carried-over Hackl: the run starts on the test
# route `hackl falkenstein` (title, the flow_hackl_carry_over inputs on
# the hackl test level, its goal and the route map), then Falkenstein is
# played as Hackl from frame 2214 with the qa_falkenstein_relaxed inputs
# (axes instead of stomps for pilgrim group A). Under the rockfall net,
# 28 frames after rock #2 (col 92) drops, one RUN press throws an axe
# that meets the falling rock at frame 4038: AxeHit, +50 (12450 -> 12500),
# no hurt, still Hackl.
# Re-cut after the QA level fixes (garden wall at col 17): the Fürberg
# stretch (frames 2214-2520) waits for the Mozartkugel under the M-box
# before the wall jump, then rejoins the original run.
